# Unity Import animation with skin note

Create Date:2026.06.01

**Meshy Export Settings**
Format FBX, Skinned Character on, Skeleton and Skinned Model, Frame Rate 30, download all files (FBX + all PNG textures)

---

**Unity Import**

1. Drag all files into the correct `Assets/Models/People/` folder

2. Click **Character_output** FBX, Rig tab, Animation Type → **Humanoid**, Avatar Definition → **Create From This Model**, click **Apply**

3. Click **Animation** FBX, Rig tab, Animation Type → **Humanoid**, Avatar Definition → **Copy From Other Avatar**, Source → select **Character_outputAvatar**, click **Apply**

---

**Animator Controller Setup**

4. Right-click in the folder, Create **Animator Controller**

5. Double-click to open, drag the animation clip into the empty area, it auto-connects to Entry

6. Click the orange state node, in Inspector drag the correct animation clip into the **Motion** slot

---

**Scene Setup**

7. Drag **Character_output** into the scene

8. Click the model in the scene, in Inspector find the **Animator** component, drag the Animator Controller into the **Controller** slot

9. Press Play